{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481727-the-ivory-priesthood","id":1481727,"title":"The Ivory Priesthood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-22T22:57:44-07:00","id":1481727,"title":"The Ivory Priesthood","content":"A quick recap:<br /> <br /> Ivory Priesthood is a secretive camp of the Silver Fangs. It is said they can communicate with the dead.<br /> When the First Wolf died to save Gaia, it learned the \u201cSecret of Death\u201d. The Ivory Priesthood is a secret society of Silver Fang Theurges who, after undergoing a series of spiritual trials and tests, begin learning these same secrets about what lies beyond the shroud of Death.<br /> <br /> Have you ever used them? Played them?<br /> Overall, how do you treat these Garou &quot;necromancers&quot;? Death-priests? Gave them Silet Strider-like ability and rites to deal wth the dead? Step sideways in to the Darl Umbra?<br /> Do you know the joke about the Ivory Priest, the Cappadocian, the Sefekhi and the Chakravanti walks in to a bar?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T03:30:51-07:00","id":1481743,"title":"","content":"The Ivory Priesthood has access to the Dark Umbra, via the Rite that is usually the Silent Striders thing. That is in the 1st Edition TB, iirc. The Rite is also prominently featured in Ghost Town, a WtO/Wild West setting book. There it is mentioned that every tribe once used the Rite but it has fallen into disuse.<br /> <br /> There is also a variant of the Death Dust Talen for the Priesthood. While the Talen usually allows for some heartbreaking goodbyes, their variant allows for questions to be asked that need to be answered truthfully. So, it is probably also effective to use on a killed enemy.<br /> <br /> Besides that, I never really used them. My first Silver Fang had ambitions to join them one day, but he was killed before he had a chance...<br /> <br /> I'd imagine them to be quite secretive, but would not really add to much necromancy to them, since it feels out of scope for my taste (in a WtA game). In a crossover game a garou being a necromancer would be an unexpected NPC...<br /> <br /> I don't know the joke. Please, tell it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T04:26:09-07:00","id":1481744,"title":"","content":"No one in my troup played them yet.<br /> Once I had one of them in a pre-christian era chronicle. It was built around omens of death/destruction/omens/sacrifice.<br /> One NPC was an extreamly shy metis of Silver Fangs, and a recently initiated Ivory Priestess. She was able to give valuable information and was good to shine light on the &quot;metis-Silver Fang rule&quot; problem.<br /> She sacrificed herself to prevent a massive bane run amok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:59:51-07:00","id":1481803,"title":"","content":"Never played one or seen any use them in game. Although I designed an NPC who is a member wom I haven't used yet.<br /> <br /> At one level, this is simply to give some Silver Fangs access to the Dark Umbra and explore the setting of Wraith. Mission accomplished. You move on.<br /> <br /> However, that is insufficient for roleplaying purposes. The Ivory Priesthood is supposed to be a small caste that preserves &quot;the Secret of Death&quot; as learned by the Progenitor Wolf. That sacred mystery is important as it should govern the actions of the members of the Ivory Priesthood. And whatever the &quot;Secret of Death&quot; is, it probably isn't to do with the Underworld and Wraiths. That does not define death, as it is really a failure of all Wraiths to be able to move on. I have no problem with the Ivory Priesthood being familiar with the Underworld and having rites or Gifts that affect that - but it should not be the purpose of the Ivory Priesthood. Which unfortunately is what it seems like if it is just used as a way to give Silver Fangs access to the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Ivory Priesthood to be very similar to the ancient Eleusinian Mysteries of Greece. That had to deal with the Greek myth of the abduction of Persephone by Hades, and her partial return to her mother Demeter - thus explaining the cycle of seasons. You can find many other similar myths (Inanna, Dionysus, Orpheus, Zalmoxis, etc.). For the initiated, the rebirth of Persephone symbolized the eternity of life which flows from generation to generation. So it would prepare its members for the death of all individual things - including themselves - but the ongoing continuity of life in Gaia. <br /> <br /> If I ever had to run a game where the Ivory Priesthood came into play, I'd read up a lot on those Mysteries and related myths and come up with details as related to the Garou, and explain to any PC that there were given additional information - which they may not actually understand yet - which is completely forbidden to tell to the uninitiated (and if they did, it would mean their death). But I would want to provide enough detail to the player that they would know how to roleplay things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T17:51:22-07:00","id":1481806,"title":"","content":"As historians and lore keepers, mainly. Mostly based around their connection to ancestor spirits, ghosts and other windows to the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}